---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';

const game = 'https://andrewnakas.github.io/skate3-cleanroom/';
---
<Base title="Play in your browser" description="Skate the Skate 3 Rust engine in your browser on WebGPU, with a clean-room asset pack: no retail files, no install.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Play" title="Skate in your browser" lede="The Skate 3 Rust and Bevy engine compiled to WebAssembly and WebGPU, with a clean-room asset pack: every texture and sound regenerated, no retail pixels shipped." />
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stage" id="stage">
      <div class="gate">
        <p><strong>Needs Chrome or Edge 113+</strong> (WebGPU). It's a large download, and the first load compiles shaders.</p>
        <button class="btn primary" type="button" id="start">Start skating</button>
        <p class="small">Or <a href={game}>open it full-page</a>.</p>
        <p class="small warn" id="nogpu" hidden>Your browser doesn't expose WebGPU. Try a recent Chrome or Edge on desktop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="info">
      <section>
        <h2>Controls</h2>
        <p>Keyboard and browser gamepads both work. A gamepad plays best: each stick does what it did on the Xbox 360. Use the map picker to switch maps, or add <code>?map=Name</code> to the full-page URL.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>What's in the pack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Regenerated:</strong> all 7,681 textures, each rebuilt from coarse facts (size, a color grid, an alpha outline) plus new detail noise, and 27 player sounds.</li>
          <li><strong>Kept, as facts:</strong> map geometry, collision, grind rails, the skater rig, animations and physics tuning.</li>
          <li><strong>Not shipped:</strong> music, speech and everything else from the disc.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A taint scan compares every regenerated file with the retail one: 0 failing. <a href="https://github.com/andrewnakas/skate3-cleanroom">How it's built →</a></p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Known limits</h2>
        <p>The three big districts (Downtown, University, Industrial) aren't in the web build yet. Web audio is a simple clean-room driver, not the desktop build's exact audio.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<script define:vars={{ game }}>
  const start = document.getElementById('start');
  if (!('gpu' in navigator)) document.getElementById('nogpu').hidden = false;
  start.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const frame = document.createElement('iframe');
    frame.src = game;
    frame.title = 'Skate 3 clean-room web build';
    frame.allow = 'fullscreen; gamepad; autoplay; cross-origin-isolated';
    frame.allowFullscreen = true;
    const stage = document.getElementById('stage');
    stage.replaceChildren(frame);
    frame.focus();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .stage {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; width: 100%; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; background: #0b0b0d;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; place-items: center;
  }
  .stage :global(iframe) { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; display: block; }
  .gate { text-align: center; padding: 1.5rem; color: #ecebe6; max-width: 44ch; }
  .gate a { color: #ffd21f; }
  .small { font-size: 0.88rem; opacity: 0.8; }
  .warn { color: #f2a94b; opacity: 1; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .stage { aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; } }
  .info { display: grid; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .info { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .info h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .info p, .info li { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .info ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; }
</style>
